<title>JAPAN: Japan MOF says plans to offer T-bills on Wednesday.</title>
<headline>Japan MOF says plans to offer T-bills on Wednesday.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Ministry of Finance (MOF) plans to offer Treasury bills through a price-competitive auction on Wednesday, a MOF official said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Traders said the MOF is likely to offer 1.2 trillion yen worth of six-month T-bills as T-bills with similar terms are maturing on March 10 and need to be rolled over.</p>
</text>
